,"On en veut pour preuve la cartographie insulaire d'André Thevet (1516- 1592), le « cosmographe » ou géographe des rois de France à partir de 1560."]],[50283,"cosmographique","adjective",0,"","","",[["cosmographic","",[],[],[]]],{"masculine":"cosmographique","masculine_plural":"cosmographiques"},[],["Table cosmographique.","Description cosmographique."]],[50284,"cosmogénique","adjective",0,"","","",[["cosmogenic","",[],[],[]]],{"masculine":"cosmogénique","masculine_plural":"cosmogéniques"},[],""],[50285,"cosmologiquement","adverb",0,"/kɔs.mɔ.lɔ.ʒik.mɑ̃/","",[37214,"LL-Q150_%28fra%29-WikiLucas00-cosmologiquement.wav.mp3"],[["cosmologically","",[],[],[]]],{},[],""],[50286,"cosmologiste","noun",0,"/kɔs.mɔ.lɔ.ʒist/","",[37215,"LL-Q150_%28fra%29-Lyoko%C3%AF-cosmologiste.wav.mp3"],[["cosmologist","",[],[],[]]],{"plural":"cosmologistes"},[],["Cela vous revient maintenant, vous savez qui était Jacques : un cosmologiste de renom."]],[50287,"cosmonucléide","noun",0,"","m","",[["cosmonuclide","",[],[],[]]],{"plural":"cosmonucléides"},[],""],[50288,"cosmopole","noun",0,"/kɔs.mɔ.pɔl/","f","",[["cosmopolis (a large city that attracts people from very diverse backgrounds, to the point that its population seems, by its composition, to represent the whole world)","",[],[],[["Ce sont eux que j'évoque dans « A Song from Exile » : ces foules venues des postes-frontières de l'Empire, de plus ou moins loin, pour chercher refuge et vengeance dans la cosmopole.","It is them whom I evoke in “A Song from Exile”: those crowds who came from the Empire's frontier posts, from near and far, to seek refuge and revenge in the cosmopolis.",""],["« Oran, une cosmopole de commerçants venus de partout, et surtout d'ailleurs, une ville étincelant dans un patchwork de mille couleurs sous le calme soleil d'Afrique du Nord. » (Yves Saint Laurent, 1983.)","Oran, a cosmopolis of merchants who came from everywhere, and above all from elsewhere, a city sparkling in a patchwork of a thousand colors beneath the tranquil North African sun.",""]]],["the world viewed as a vast cosmopolitan city","",[],[],[["Au sein d'une cosmopole mondialisée, des identités ethniques, linguistiques et religieuses, au caractère perturbateur, se font valoir par l'usage insolite des moyens de violence qui remettent en cause la légitimité des États et celle du système des États.","Within a globalized cosmopolis, ethnic, linguistic, and religious identities, disruptive in character, assert themselves through the unusual use of violent means that calls into question the legitimacy of states and that of the state system.",""]]]],{"plural":"cosmopoles"},[],""],[50289,"cosmétiquer","verb",0,"/kɔs.me.ti.ke/","",[37216,"LL-Q150_%28fra%29-Lyoko%C3%AF-cosm%C3%A9tiquer.wav.mp3"],[["to make up (apply cosmetics)","",[],[],[]]],{"infinitive":"cosmétiquer","auxiliary":"avoir","present_participle":"cosmétiquant","past_participle":"cosmétiqué","present":["cosmétique","cosmétiques","cosmétique","cosmétiquons","cosmétiquez","cosmétiquent"],"imperfect":["cosmétiquais","cosmétiquais","cosmétiquait","cosmétiquions","cosmétiquiez","cosmétiquaient"],"future":["cosmétiquerai","cosmétiqueras","cosmétiquera","cosmétiquerons","cosmétiquerez","cosmétiqueront"],"conditional":["cosmétiquerais","cosmétiquerais","cosmétiquerait","cosmétiquerions","cosmétiqueriez","cosmétiqueraient"],"subjunctive":["cosmétique","cosmétiques","cosmétique","cosmétiquions","cosmétiquiez","cosmétiquent"]},[],["En face de lui, derrière le comptoir, M. Henri, rasé, poudré, cosmétiqué, paraissait par contraste presque chétif."]],[50290,"cosom hockey","noun",0,"","m","",[["cosom hockey; alternative form of hockey cosom","",["uncountable"],[],[]]],{},[],""],[50291,"cosplay","noun",0,"/kɔs.plɛ/","m",[37217,"LL-Q150_%28fra%29-DSwissK-cosplay.wav.mp3"],[["cosplay","",[],["costumade"],[]]],{"plural":"cosplays"},[],["Au Japon, les défilés de cosplay sont très prisés par les jeunes.","Dans le cadre du festival Anima se déroulait ce dimanche à Flagey, un conco